# libretranslate
msgid "**An agent can be provisioned with its own platform user account.** Creating an agent employee optionally provisions a dedicated identity through the platform's existing user mechanism (the `users` lookup, LDAP via [`svc-db-openldap`](../../roles/svc-db-openldap/), SSO via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/)); no new account system is built. The account is a **non-privileged standard user** by default (never administrator/service-account-with-mutating-tools). When enabled, the agent authenticates as its own user: OIDC login to its dashboard, a distinct mailbox/identity, and MCP calls made with `auth_subject: user` ([025](025-mcp-role-integration.md)) scoped to that account rather than a shared service account. The account is opt-in per agent; its password/token lives in the role's `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` block, never in README or env. An agent MUST also be deployable against an existing account (no forced account creation)."
msgstr "**En agent kan leveres med sin egen platform bruger konto.** Oprettelse af en agent medarbejder frivilligt leverer en dedikeret identitet gennem platformens eksisterende brugermekanisme (i `users` lookup, LDAP via [`svc-db-openldap`](../../roles/svc-db-openldap/), SSO via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/)); ingen nye konto system er bygget. Kontoen er **ikke-privilegeret standardbruger** som standard (aldrig administrator / service-account-with-mutation-tools). Når det er aktiveret, bekræfter agenten som sin egen bruger: OIDC login til sit dashboard, en særskilt postkasse / identitet, og MCP opkald foretaget med `auth_subject: user` ([025](025-mcp-role-integration.md)) kobles til denne konto i stedet for en delt servicekonto. Kontoen er opt- in per agent; dens password / token lever i rollens `meta/secrets.yml` `credentials:` Block, aldrig i README eller env. En agent SKAL også kunne indsættes på en eksisterende konto (ingen oprettelse af tvangskonti)."

# libretranslate
msgid "**An engine inside its consumer's project** — matrix with its own postgres, for instance — is started service by service rather than as a whole project, because bringing the project up would start the consumer and the chain refuses to replay while one runs. The discriminator is the dump's volume name against its project name: equal for the central engines (`postgres` in project `postgres`), different for a per-app one (`matrix_database` in project `matrix`)."
msgstr "**En motor i forbrugerens projekt** - matrix med sine egne postgres, for eksempel - er startet service af service snarere end som et hele projekt, fordi bringe projektet op ville starte forbrugeren og kæden nægter at spille igen, mens man kører. Diskriminatoren er dummens volumennavn mod projektets navn: lige for de centrale motorer (`postgres` i projekt `postgres`), anderledes for en per- app en (`matrix_database` i projekt `matrix`)."

