msgid "**Independent of docker:** Docker owns its own tables and never touches these, so no rule has to be inserted into a chain another component controls. The unit is only enabled, never started or restarted: on Debian its ``ExecStop`` flushes the entire ruleset, docker’s tables included, and the fragments are loaded explicitly anyway."
msgstr "**Uafhængig af docker:** Docker ejer sine egne borde og rører dem aldrig, så ingen regel skal indsættes i en kæde en anden komponent kontrol. Enheden er kun aktiveret, aldrig startet eller genstartet: på Debian its ``ExecStop`` flugter hele regelet, docker tabeller inkluderet, og fragmenter er indlæst eksplicit alligevel."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Infinito.Nexus** is an **automated, modular infrastructure framework** built on **Docker**, **Linux**, and **Ansible**, equally suited for cloud services, local server management, and desktop workstations. At its core lies a **web-based desktop with single sign-on**, backed by an **LDAP directory** and **OIDC**, granting **seamless access** to an almost limitless portfolio of self-hosted applications. It fully supports **ActivityPub applications** and is **Fediverse-compatible**, while integrated **monitoring**, **alerting**, **cleanup**, **self-healing**, **automated updates**, and **backup solutions** provide everything an organization needs to run at scale."
msgstr "**Infinito.Nexus** er et **Automatiske, modulære infrastrukturrammer** bygget på **Docker**, **Linux**, og **Ansible**, lige velegnet til cloud-tjenester, lokal server management, og desktop arbejdsstationer. I sin kerne ligger en **web- baseret desktop med enkelt sign- on**, med **LDAP- mappe** og **OIDC**, ydelse **problemfri adgang** til en næsten ubegrænset portefølje af egne applikationer. Det støtter fuldt ud **ActivityPub applikationer** og er **Fediverse- kompatibel**, mens integreret **overvågning**, **alarmering**, **oprydning**, **selv- healing**, **automatiserede opdateringer**, og **backup-løsninger** give alt, hvad en organisation behøver for at køre i skala."

