# libretranslate
msgid "**Multisite Management:** Easily create and maintain multiple sites with a single WordPress installation, ideal for networks of blogs, corporate intranets, or educational institutions."
msgstr "**Multisite Management:** Nemt at oprette og vedligeholde flere sites med en enkelt WordPress installation, ideel til netværk af blogs, corporate intranets, eller uddannelsesinstitutioner."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Multisite path** (auto-detected via `is_multisite()`): per-site roles come from `/roles/web-app-wordpress/<canonical-domain>/<role>` entries; the super-admin capability comes from `/roles/web-app-wordpress/network-administrator`. The mapper adds the user to any site they have a role for (`add_user_to_blog`) and removes them from sites it previously added them to (`remove_user_from_blog`) when a role for that site disappears from the claim. A user-meta marker (`_infinito_oidc_added_blog_ids`) records which blog memberships the mapper owns, so memberships added through `wp-admin` or the REST API outside the OIDC flow are never touched."
msgstr "**Multisite sti** (autodetekteret via `is_multisite()`): per- site roller kommer fra `/roles/web-app-wordpress/<canonical-domain>/<role>` poster; super- admin evnen kommer fra `/roles/web-app-wordpress/network-administrator`. Den mapper tilføjer brugeren til ethvert websted, de har en rolle for (`add_user_to_blog`) og fjerner dem fra websteder, det tidligere tilføjet dem til (`remove_user_from_blog`) når en rolle for dette sted forsvinder fra kravet. En bruger- meta markør (`_infinito_oidc_added_blog_ids`) poster, som blog medlemskaber mapperen ejer, så medlemskaber tilføjet gennem `wp-admin` eller REST API uden for OIDC strømmen er aldrig rørt."

