# libretranslate
msgid "**Not every subject is a compose project.** Discourse is built by its own `./launcher rebuild` ([handlers/stack_host.yml](../../../web-app-discourse/handlers/stack_host.yml)) and runs as a plain container with no compose label. The drill treats such a container as a subject whenever it mounts a volume this generation backed up: it is stopped with everything else and started again at the end, and its return is asserted like any other. Left running it would take an `rsync --delete` into its live data directory, and the chain's consumer check — which reads compose labels — would not see it, so the dump replay would race it exactly like the zammad failure this whole change came from."
msgstr "**Ikke alle emner er et komponistprojekt.** Diskursen er bygget af sin egen `./launcher rebuild` ([handlers/stack_host.yml](../../../web-app-discourse/handlers/stack_host.yml)) og kører som en almindelig beholder uden at komponere etiket. Boret behandler en sådan beholder som et emne, når det opstøver en volumen denne generation bakket op: det er stoppet med alt andet og startede igen i slutningen, og dets tilbagevenden er hævdet som enhver anden. Venstre kører det ville kræve en `rsync --delete` i sin live data mappe, og kædens forbruger check - som læser etiketter - ville ikke se det, så dump replay ville race det præcis ligesom zammad fiasko denne ændring kom fra."

