# libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**   When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT's native `loginViaRemoteUser()` is enabled via the `Setting` model (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx gates `/login` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` header, which Snipe-IT matches against `users.username` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native `snipeit_session`. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (`login_common_disabled = 0`), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "**Trusted- Header SSO Bridge:** Når oauth2-proxy SSO smag er aktiv, Snipe- IT 's indfødte `loginViaRemoteUser()` er aktiveret via `Setting` model (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx porte `/login` gennem oauth2-proxy / Keycloak og injicerer verificeret `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` header, som Snipe- IT matcher mod `users.username` (brugeren skal præeksistere og aktiveres - synkronisere dem via LDAP) at male en indfødt `snipeit_session`. Besøgende uden en matchende aktiveret bruger lydløst falde igennem til den normale login form (ingen fejl). Adgangskoden / LDAP login formular forbliver tilgængelig som en fallback (`login_common_disabled = 0`), og in- app logout er omdirigeret til den centrale OIDC end- session URL."

# libretranslate
