# libretranslate
msgid "By default — for an **untrusted** fork PR — the privileged `pull_request_target` build checks out the **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) from the base repository: the PR's changes merged onto base, with all workflow and build-orchestration scripts coming from base, never from the fork. Because `actions/checkout` otherwise refuses to fetch a PR ref under `pull_request_target`, the source checkout sets `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. The untrusted build runs **without organization secrets** — `secrets: inherit` is not passed and it authenticates to GHCR with the per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN` only, so a malicious fork cannot read repository/organization secrets. (The `pull_request_target` token still carries `packages: write`, so the `🛡️ Trusted` label remains the real trust boundary for anything beyond image publication.)"
msgstr "Som standard - for en **ikke betroet** gaffel PR - de privilegerede `pull_request_target` bygge kontrol ud af **basisfletningsref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) fra base repository: PR 's ændringer fusioneret til base, med alle workflow og build- orkestreringsscripts kommer fra base, aldrig fra gaflen. Fordi `actions/checkout` ellers nægter at hente en PR-ref under `pull_request_target`, kildekontrolsæt `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. De ubetroede build runs **uden organisationshemmeligheder** - `secrets: inherit` er ikke bestået, og det autentificerer til GHCR med per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN` kun, så en ondsindet gaffel ikke kan læse lagerhemmeligheder / organisation hemmeligheder. (Den `pull_request_target` token stadig bærer `packages: write`, så `🛡️ Trusted` mærkning forbliver den virkelige tillid grænse for noget ud over billedet offentliggørelse.)"

