# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw exposes no administrator-visible list of configured MCP servers, so the configured set is proven by a CLI test instead: [`files/test/test.sh`](./files/test/test.sh) probes the agent's `mcp` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a `failed to start server` line. The Playwright spec covers the complementary case, that the gateway holding the MCP credentials refuses an unauthenticated caller."
msgstr "OpenClaw udsætter ingen administrator- synlig liste over konfigurerede MCP-servere, så det indstillede sæt er bevist ved en CLI-test i stedet: [`files/test/test.sh`](./files/test/test.sh) sonder agentens `mcp` overflade og mislykkes, når exec selv mislykkes eller output bærer en `failed to start server` Linje. Den Playwright spec dækker den supplerende sag, at den gateway, der holder MCP legitimationsoplysninger nægter en ikke-godkendt opkald."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw exposes no administrator-visible list of configured MCP servers, so the configured set is proven by a CLI test instead: ```files/test/test.sh`` <./files/test/test.sh>`__ probes the agent’s ``mcp`` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a ``failed to start server`` line. The Playwright spec covers the complementary case, that the gateway holding the MCP credentials refuses an unauthenticated caller."
msgstr "OpenClaw udsætter ingen administrator- synlig liste over konfigurerede MCP-servere, så det indstillede sæt er bevist ved en CLI-test i stedet: ```files/test/test.sh`` <./files/test/test.sh>`__ probes the agent’s ``mcp`` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a ``failed to start server`` Linje. Den Playwright spec dækker den supplerende sag, at den gateway, der holder MCP legitimationsoplysninger nægter en ikke-godkendt opkald."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw's own CLI reference says so directly: `openclaw mcp serve` \"starts a stdio MCP server\" whose process \"the MCP client owns\". Every HTTP transport in that document belongs to the opposite direction, `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, which is OpenClaw acting as a client. Hermes is the same shape: both entry points, `mcp_serve.py` and `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, run the MCP SDK's stdio transport, the repository defines neither `run_streamable_http_async` nor `sse_app`, and the user-facing MCP guide describes only Hermes consuming external servers."
msgstr "OpenClaws egen CLI-reference siger det direkte: `openclaw mcp serve` \"starter en stdio MCP server\" hvis proces \"MCP-klienten ejer\". Hver HTTP-transport i dette dokument tilhører den modsatte retning, `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, Det er OpenClaw, der fungerer som kunde. Hermes er den samme form: begge indgange, `mcp_serve.py` og `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, køre MCP SDK s stdio transport, lageret definerer hverken `run_streamable_http_async` eller `sse_app`, og brugervendt MCP guide beskriver kun Hermes forbrugende eksterne servere."

