msgstr "Returnerer Sandt hvis programmer[application_id]Tjenesteydelser[service_name].aktiveret er sandy, ellers returnerer False (også hvis mellemnøgler mangler)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns True if the docker service flag is enabled for this application."
msgstr "Returnerer Sandt hvis docker service flag er aktiveret for dette program."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns True when the stderr of a failed ``docker network connect|disconnect`` only reports an idempotent no-op: the endpoint already is in the desired state ('connect') or the network/container to detach from is absent ('disconnect'). Any other daemon error (permissions, dead daemon, active endpoints) stays False so the caller's failed_when still trips."
msgstr "Returnerer Sandt, når stderr af en mislykkedes ``docker network connect|disconnect`` kun rapporterer en idempotent no- op: endepunktet allerede er i den ønskede tilstand ('connect') eller netværket / beholderen til at løsne sig fra er fraværende ('disconnect')Enhver anden dæmon fejl (tilladelser, døde dæmoner, aktive endepunkter) forbliver False så ringer failed_when Stadig ture."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns True when the stderr of a failed ``gitea admin auth add-ldap|add-oauth`` only reports that the login source already exists; any other CLI error stays False so the caller's failed_when still trips."
msgstr "Returnerer Sandt, når stderr af en mislykkedes ``gitea admin auth add-ldap|add-oauth`` kun rapporter om, at login-kilden allerede eksisterer; enhver anden CLI fejl forbliver False, så den ringer failed_when Stadig ture."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns True when the stderr of a failed ldapmodify/ldapadd only reports that the attribute, value or entry already exists; any other LDAP error stays False so the caller's failed_when still trips."
msgstr "Returnerer Sandt, når stderr af en mislykket ldapmodification / ldapadd kun rapporterer, at attributten, værdi eller indgang allerede eksisterer; enhver anden LDAP fejl forbliver False, så opkalderen er failed_when Stadig ture."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns ``(entries, trailing)`` where ``entries`` is a list of ``(version, date, body)`` tuples and ``trailing`` is everything after the last version entry that opens with an archive header."
msgstr "Returnerer ``(entries, trailing)`` hvor ``entries`` er en liste over ``(version, date, body)`` tupler og ``trailing`` er alt efter den sidste version indgang, der åbnes med en arkivoverskrift."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns ``(kept, archive_paths)`` where ``archive_paths`` is the list of newly-written or to-be-written archive files (empty when no entry was displaced past *keep*)."
msgstr "Returnerer ``(kept, archive_paths)`` hvor ``archive_paths`` er listen over ny- skrevne eller to- be- skrevne arkivfiler (tom når ingen adgang blev fordrevet forbi *Behold*)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns ``None`` when neither key is declared, which is what the coverage lint reports as a gap."
msgstr "Returnerer ``None`` når der ikke angives nogen nøgle, hvilket er, hvad dækningen lint rapporterer som et hul."

# libretranslate
msgid "Returns ``True`` when the file was rewritten, ``False`` when nothing happened (no entries or dry run)."
msgstr "Returnerer ``True`` når filen blev omskrevet ``False`` når intet skete (ingen indgange eller tørløb)."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Returns ``[{id, canonical_domain, canonical_url, iframe}, …]`` for every role whose merged applications config declares ``services.<service>.{enabled, shared}`` as truthy. ``iframe`` reflects ``services.<service>.iframe`` (defaulting to ``enabled``) so consumers can tell embeddable cards from those that must open in a new tab."
msgstr "Returnerer ``[{id, canonical_domain, canonical_url, iframe}, …]`` for hver rolle hvis fusionerede applikationer config erklærer ``services.<service>.{enabled, shared}`` som sandy. ``iframe`` afspejler ``services.<service>.iframe`` (misligholdende ``enabled``) så forbrugerne kan fortælle indlejrede kort fra dem, der skal åbne i en ny fane."

